<h1>Threat Model and Secure Configuration</h1>
<p class="mut">Target: <b>NoteBox</b>, a small web app where users sign up, log in, write private notes, attach files, and get password-reset emails. Defensive analysis only.</p>

<h2>1. Scope and assumptions</h2>
<div class="card"><ul>
<li><b>Stack:</b> browser SPA, Node/Express API, PostgreSQL, object storage for attachments, third-party email service (e.g. SendGrid), hosted on a cloud VM behind a reverse proxy.</li>
<li><b>Users:</b> anonymous visitors, registered users, one admin.</li>
<li><b>Assets:</b> user credentials, private notes, session tokens, uploaded files, API/DB secrets, availability of the service.</li>
<li><b>Attackers considered:</b> opportunistic internet scanners, a malicious registered user, someone who steals a user's password from another breach.</li>
</ul></div>

